    description: "MEASURED on a fixture with positive controls firing in the same run. js_ts.py:777 carries JS_KNOWN_GLOBALS, a HAND-MAINTAINED mirror of the same class as python's EXTERNAL_CONSTRUCTOR_TYPES, and it has drifted: 'process' is absent though process.send/process.on match the bare-global Object.method() pattern its own comment describes, and 'new WebSocket(...)' receivers produce no edge at all.\n\nRELEVANT TO THE SECOND-LANGUAGE REQUIREMENT: JS/TS is the likeliest language in participants' repos (83 sinks vs TypeScript's 6). This is a recall hole in it.\n\nNOT VERIFIED whether process's absence is deliberate -- the surrounding comment reads as though it should be included."  # 4dc3
